## Context

Requirement Q17 (`docs/jetp-requirements.md`) and extraction § 6.3
(`docs/jetp-extraction.md`) make the reference answers "made by hand blind
to any machine reading" the only human check on the readers. The survey
(`conception/jetp-m2-3-reading-design-survey-2026-10-01.md` § 6) counted
the existing non-comparator lines and found:

- Finding: the existing lines were made by agents, not by a person blind to
  a machine reading. R1 (130 lines) comes from the 0970 and 1160
  reconciliations, whose tickets name Codex as author; R2 (233) has no
  recorded provenance; R3 (112) is anchored in a ledger CSV, not in the
  publisher's document; P (2,165) is parser output. Calibrating the readers
  against them would be circular. Agent-made lines may serve only as a
  secondary tuning set, never as held-out reference answers.
- The set is also thin where the work is: Viet Nam has 0 held-out items,
  South Africa 26, transcription 0; every French, Indonesian-language and
  Vietnamese stratum is under 30. South Africa and Viet Nam hold 74 of the
  115 pending documents.

Author decision (2026-10-01, interactive): build a small human gold set.

## Scope target

About 10 to 15 documents and about 300 to 500 lines, stratified by country
(ZAF, IDN, VNM, SEN) x language x statement shape (table row, record page,
prose span, transcription). Viet Nam and South Africa are weighted up.

Sizing rule: the spec fixes a seeded split but no proportion. Under a 50/50
split a stratum needs 60 lines to reach 30 held-out items. The proportion is
itself a decision to record with the seed (a 40/60 tuning/held-out split
needs 50 lines per stratum, but leaves prompt writing less to read).

Draft sizing, at 50/50 (about 450 lines in all):

| Stratum | Lines | Held-out | Reaches 30? |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| VNM, Vietnamese, prose span | 60 | 30 | yes |
| VNM, Vietnamese, table row | 60 | 30 | yes |
| VNM, Vietnamese, record page | 10 | 5 | no, named uncalibrated |
| VNM, English or unrecorded language, any shape | 20 | 10 | no, named uncalibrated |
| ZAF, English, table row | 60 | 30 | yes |
| ZAF, English, prose span | 60 | 30 | yes |
| ZAF, English, record page | 30 | 15 | no, named uncalibrated (pooled) |
| SEN, French, prose span | 60 | 30 | yes |
| IDN, English, prose span | 30 | 15 | no, named uncalibrated |
| Transcription (the one scan) | 60 | 30 | only if the scan carries 60 lines; else named |
| **Total** | **450** | **225** | |

Strata that cannot reach 30 held-out items in this budget, to be named in
the closing report and run under the fallback of extraction § 6.3: Indonesia
(all shapes), Senegal table rows and record pages, South Africa record
pages, Viet Nam record pages and non-Vietnamese Viet Nam documents, and
Indonesian-language documents as a language (the pending Indonesia
documents are English or have no recorded language). Reaching them costs
about 60 more lines each; that is the author's call on the size.

## Method

- Blind: the annotator never sees a machine reading of the document (no
  proposal, parser row, ledger line, or earlier agent note). A document
  that already has R1/R2/R3/P lines is read from the source alone.
- Selection: documents drawn from the pending plus the held documents by a
  recorded seed, per stratum, stratified as above.
- Split: a tuning part and a held-out part by a second recorded seed,
  stratified by language and statement shape, before any prompt writing.
- Extraction against the ontology, never in a vacuum: the field list per
  document type (`data/jetp/line-field-specs.csv`), closed lists from
  `data/jetp/ontology/terms.csv` (the 13 classifications and the closed
  value lists), and for anything outside the lists an `other` slot with a
  verbatim quote.
- Each line carries a verbatim quote and its page or cell; locators are
  derived from the quotes and checked by code afterwards (extraction § 5
  and § 6.3), so the annotator copies text and does not compute offsets.
- The lines take the readers' output format, so that scoring needs no
  re-anchoring.

## Who annotates (open decision, needs-human)

The author or a paid annotator. The annotator must read Vietnamese, French
and English; the Vietnamese strata (about 150 lines) are the binding
constraint.

Estimate (derived, not measured): 450 lines at 3 to 4 minutes per line,
including reading around the line and the ontology lookup, is 22 to 30
hours; plus 3 hours for the kit walkthrough and a pilot of 20 lines, 3
hours for locator-check fixes and a second look at flagged lines, and 2
hours for questions on Vietnamese terms: 30 to 38 hours in all. A paid
annotator with Vietnamese takes the same hours plus about 3 hours of
briefing by the author. Vietnamese table rows may run slower at first.

## Draft selection proposal (read-only, from `data/jetp/`)

Derivation, a draft to be redone by the kit step: the pending pool was
rebuilt as documents that are active, have a collected retrieval, have no
non-comparator line on their snapshot, and are not bulk data (CSV, JSON,
gzip, JavaScript). It gives 111 documents, not the survey's 115, so the
survey's authoritative list must be reconciled before the draw is final
(`documents.csv` has no format column; the format is the snapshot content
type). Pool by country and language: VNM 20 vi, 4 en, 1 unrecorded; ZAF 43
en, 6 unrecorded; SEN 15 fr, 5 en, 4 unrecorded; IDN 7 en, 6 unrecorded.
The scan for the transcription stratum is not identified here.

Seeded draw, `random.Random(1891).sample` over the sorted pool of each
cell, 15 documents:

| Cell | Pool | Drawn |
|---|---:|---|
| VNM vi prose span | 13 | vnm-moit-newsletter-12-2026-02, vnm-moit-newsletter-01-2025-03, vnm-moit-newsletter-13-2026-03 |
| VNM vi table row | 2 | vnm-decision-1009-2023, vnm-rmp-2023-vi |
| VNM vi record page | 3 | vnm-moit-project-binh-duong-dong-nai |
| ZAF en table row | 3 | zaf-jet-pmu-projects, zaf-jet-grants-register-2024-q2 |
| ZAF en prose span | 15 | zaf-jet-grants-faq-2025-q1, zaf-jetp-leaders-2022, zaf-jet-quarterly-2025-q2 |
| ZAF en record page | 13 | zaf-kfw-jetp-project-profile |
| SEN fr prose span | 6 | sen-boad-signed-instruments-2024, sen-uasz-vev-thesis-2024 |
| IDN en prose span | 6 | idn-jetp-guarantees-insurance-2025 |

Cell definitions used: prose span = progress updates, annual reports and
plans; table row = project lists, investment and implementation plans;
record page = project pages. Caveats: a document's yield is unknown until
read, so each cell may need a reserve document; vnm-rmp-2023-vi overlaps a
parser family (RMP annexes) and must be read from the source only; this is
a proposal, and the kit step records the seed and the final list.

## Spec errata (propose to the author; the spec is not edited here)

Extraction § 6.3, "Reference answers, the only human check", says: "The
reference answers are the lines of the extracted documents made by hand
blind to any machine reading (requirement Q17)". That wording implies that
hand-made lines of extracted documents already exist. That is factually
wrong: the existing lines were made by agents (survey § 6). The author is
asked to amend the wording to name a dedicated set, for example: "The
reference answers are a gold set that a person builds blind to any machine
reading, from documents drawn by a recorded seed (ticket 1895); lines made
by agents or parsers are a secondary tuning set only." The same check
applies to the matching sentences of requirement Q17 and operation § 5.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The author decides who annotates (author or paid annotator) and the
  tuning/held-out proportion; the choice is logged here
- [ ] Selection and seed are recorded: the final document list drawn from
  the pending plus held documents, reconciled with the survey's 115, with
  the seed and the reserve documents
- [ ] The annotation kit is ready: per document the text layer, the field
  list, the closed lists from `terms.csv`, an `other` slot with quote, and
  no machine reading of that document
- [ ] Annotation is done, blind
- [ ] The locator check passes, or the failures are fixed
- [ ] The split is recorded by a seed, and the held-out part is sealed: its
  hash is committed in the repo, and no prompt writing or model selection
  reads it
- [ ] Stratum counts are reported per country x language x shape, naming
  the strata under 30 held-out items
- [ ] A spec amendment of extraction § 6.3 (and Q17, operation § 5 where
  they repeat it) is proposed to the author, per the errata above
- [ ] The logs of [[1890]] and [[1873]] record that this ticket is
  delivered
